# Hybrid Microsoft Entra Join & Intune Troubleshooting Lab

## Overview

This lab focused on troubleshooting identity, compliance, device management, and Hybrid Microsoft Entra Join across a Windows enterprise environment.

Technologies used:

- Windows Server Active Directory
- Windows 11
- Microsoft Entra ID
- Microsoft Entra Connect Sync
- Microsoft Intune
- PowerShell
- Windows Task Scheduler

The lab began with an Intune compliance issue and eventually uncovered an important distinction between:

- User identity
- Device identity
- Active Directory domain membership
- Microsoft Entra device registration
- Intune device management

By the end of the lab, the Windows 11 client `COMP01` was successfully configured as a **Hybrid Microsoft Entra joined device** while remaining joined to the on-premises Active Directory domain and managed through Microsoft Intune.

---

# Lab Architecture

The environment consists of an on-premises Active Directory domain connected to Microsoft Entra ID through Microsoft Entra Connect.

```text
On-Premises Active Directory
aden.local
│
├── Users
│   └── jsmith
│
└── Computers
    └── COMP01
         │
         ├──── Domain Join ──────────────► Active Directory
         │
         ├──── Hybrid Entra Join ────────► Microsoft Entra ID
         │
         └──── MDM Enrollment ───────────► Microsoft Intune
```

Microsoft Entra Connect provides synchronization between the on-premises Active Directory environment and Microsoft Entra ID.

