# Part 4 - Investigating the jsmith Identity

The test user was inspected on the domain controller using PowerShell:

```powershell
Get-ADUser jsmith -Properties UserPrincipalName |
Select Name,SamAccountName,UserPrincipalName
```

The output confirmed that `jsmith` existed in Active Directory.

The Active Directory UPN suffix configuration was also inspected:

```powershell
Get-ADForest | Select -ExpandProperty UPNSuffixes
```

The user was then inspected in Microsoft Entra ID.

Microsoft Entra showed:

```text
On-premises sync enabled: Yes
```

This established that `jsmith` was already a synchronized hybrid identity.

Conceptually:

```text
Active Directory
jsmith
   │
   │ Microsoft Entra Connect
   ▼
Microsoft Entra ID
jsmith
```

The Active Directory and Microsoft Entra representations belong to the same synchronized identity.

